The Nautilus DevOps team aims to establish a ReplicaSet to deploy multiple pods for hosting applications requiring a highly available infrastructure. 
Here are the specific details to create the ReplicaSet:


a.) Create a ReplicaSet using the nginx image with the latest tag.

b.) Name the ReplicaSet nginx-replicaset-t3q5.

c.) Ensure all pods are in the Running state after deployment.

d.) The ReplicaSet should manage 3 replicas (adjustable based on your needs).

e.) The pods managed by the ReplicaSet should have the label app: nginx-t3q5.

Note: The kubectl utility on jump-host has been configured to work with the Kubernetes cluster.

ReplicaSet 'nginx-replicaset-t3q5' exists

Image used is 'nginx'

Pods are 'Running'

SOLUTION
Step 1: Create the ReplicaSet template file
Create a file (e.g., /home/thor/nginx-replicaset-t3q5.yml) with the following content:

yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: ReplicaSet
metadata:
  name: nginx-replicaset-t3q5
  labels:
    app: nginx-t3q5
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx-t3q5
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx-t3q5
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx:latest
          ports:
            - containerPort: 80
You can create it with a heredoc:

bash
cat <<'EOF' > /home/thor/nginx-replicaset-t3q5.yml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: ReplicaSet
metadata:
  name: nginx-replicaset-t3q5
  labels:
    app: nginx-t3q5
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx-t3q5
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx-t3q5
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx:latest
          ports:
            - containerPort: 80
EOF
⚠️ Critical: For a ReplicaSet, the spec.selector.matchLabels must match the pod template's metadata.labels. If they don't, the API server rejects the object. Also note apiVersion: apps/v1 (not v1) — ReplicaSets live under apps/v1.

Step 2: Apply the ReplicaSet
bash
kubectl apply -f /home/thor/nginx-replicaset-t3q5.yml
Expected output:

text
replicaset.apps/nginx-replicaset-t3q5 created
Or equivalently:

bash
kubectl create -f /home/thor/nginx-replicaset-t3q5.yml
Step 3: Verify the ReplicaSet
bash
kubectl get replicaset nginx-replicaset-t3q5
Expected output (once pods are ready):

text
NAME                     DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE
nginx-replicaset-t3q5    3         3         3       ...
Step 4: Verify the pods are running
bash
kubectl get pods -l app=nginx-t3q5
Expected output:

text
NAME                           READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE
nginx-replicaset-t3q5-xxxxx    1/1     Running   0          ...
nginx-replicaset-t3q5-yyyyy    1/1     Running   0          ...
nginx-replicaset-t3q5-zzzzz    1/1     Running   0          ...
Step 5: Confirm the image
bash
kubectl get replicaset nginx-replicaset-t3q5 -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}'
Expected output:

text
nginx:latest
